TITLE:: ArrangerView
SUMMARY:: Flow of sequence-name labels for the SequencerGui Arrange page.
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events
RELATED:: Classes/SequencerGui, Classes/SCViewHolder

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::ArrangerView:: is a LINK::Classes/SCViewHolder:: that LINK::Classes/SequencerGui:: shows when the Arrange button is pressed. Its view uses a LINK::Classes/FlowLayout:: decorator. Each sequence name is a LINK::Classes/StaticText:: sized to that name, placed beside the previous label.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates an instance of TELETYPE::ArrangerView::.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::ArrangerView:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: addSequence
Adds a label for CODE::name::. A name that is already shown is left as it is.

ARGUMENT:: name
A LINK::Classes/Symbol::, displayed with CODE::asString::.

PRIVATE:: init
